<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanesatake</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kanesatake is a Mohawk community on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottawa">Ottawa</a> river west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montreal">Montreal</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a>, next to the town of Oka. It originated in a Sulpician mission founded in the early 18th century, and its people's long dispute over land with the Sulpicians and the town led in 1990 to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oka-crisis">Oka crisis</a>, a 78-day armed stand-off over plans to extend a golf course onto a Mohawk burial ground.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanesatake.jpg" alt="Kanesatake" width="320" height="173" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gordalmighty · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanesatake_Quebec_location_diagram.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
